## Field Operations — Fail Fast on Auth / Connectivity

Scott often sends commands from the field (job sites, in transit). If any external service,
MCP tool, or API is unavailable or needs re-authentication, **do not hang or retry silently**.
Fail immediately and message back with a clear, actionable status.

**Rule: If a tool/service doesn't respond within ~10 seconds, or returns 401/403/000:**
1. Stop — do not attempt to work around it or wait
2. Reply immediately with the service name, what failed, and what Scott can do:

| Failure | Reply |
|---------|-------|
| MCP server not connected | "⚠️ [Service] MCP isn't connected right now. Reconnect via Claude Code settings or try again at the office." |
| Token expired / 401 | "⚠️ [Service] needs re-authentication — token expired. [Where to refresh]." |
| No network / timeout | "⚠️ Can't reach [Service] — no network or service is down. Try again when you're back online." |
| Missing credential | "⚠️ [Service] isn't set up yet — [credential] is missing. Scott can add it from [location]." |

**Never let a skill hang waiting for a service.** A fast "needs auth" reply is always better
than silence. Scott can handle it from the office; he can't fix a hung agent from the field.

**Per-service quick references:**
- CompanyCam: token at `~/.companycam-token`, refresh at app.companycam.com → Settings → API
- Google Calendar: `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp/tokens.json`, re-auth via `npm run auth` from `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp`
- Supabase: `.env` file in uhsJARVIS, no token expiry (anon key is permanent)
- Microsoft/Outlook: `mcp__microsoft-mcp__authenticate_account`, use `https://microsoft.com/devicelogin`
- Stageforce: Playwright session, login via `~/.companycam-token` companion credentials
- GoHighLevel: API key in `.env`, no expiry

