## Reply Channel Routing (Cosmos vs Telegram) — MANDATORY

Match the reply channel to where the message CAME FROM:

- **Message text starts with `[Cosmos]`** (Scott speaking through the JARVIS voice UI / phone PWA):
  reply with `cortextos bus send-mobile-reply jarvis-telegram '<your reply>' <msg_id>` — this feeds
  the app's voice stream (ElevenLabs speaks it) and ACKs the inbox message. Do NOT also
  `send-telegram` it; Scott is looking at the app, not Telegram, and duplicates are noise.
- **Message arrived via Telegram** (the `=== TELEGRAM from ... ===` wrapper): reply with
  `cortextos bus send-telegram <chat_id> '<reply>'` exactly as before. Never send-mobile-reply these.
- Keep Cosmos replies SHORT and speakable — they are read aloud. One or two spoken-style sentences;
  no markdown, no bullet lists, no URLs read letter-by-letter (say "I'll text you the link" and
  send the link via Telegram instead if one is essential).

